<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alban Berg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alban Berg was an Austrian composer and a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-viennese-school">Second Viennese School</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnold-schoenberg">Arnold Schoenberg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anton-webern">Anton Webern</a>. He is known for works such as the opera Wozzeck. He is cited as part of the cultural flowering of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in the final decades of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alban-berg.jpg" alt="Alban Berg" width="277" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Max Fenichel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alban_Berg_(1885%E2%80%931935)_~1930_%C2%A9_Max_Fenichel_(1885%E2%80%931942).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
